#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows-cygwin.rst:172
#: 1eabc45bdf354cd68d462e1cbbe6a29a
msgid "Build SITL binaries for Windows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows-cygwin.rst:174
#: 596fe42d257040379d552a4b44af7aae
msgid "You can build 32-bit binaries to be run outside of Cygwin with a small set of companion files. This can be useful when used in conjunction with Mission Planner to run SITL with a stable release build rather than a build from the development branch of ArduPilot. This can be done by compiling using the command below in Cygwin and copying the binary the \"sitl\" folder typically found at C:\\\\Users\\\\user\\\\Documents\\\\Mission Planner\\\\sitl. Mission Planner will download the required files during the first time running SITL. After the initial run, the vehicle-specific binary file can be replaced with the file you built. The custom SITL binaries should be located at /ardupilot/build/sitl."
msgstr ""
